cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mal-agent: Evidence-Grounded Agentic Malware Triage with Bounded LLM Adjudication"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata
  below. If you use the accompanying research (dataset v2,
  evaluation harness, or reported results), please also cite the
  paper once published (see docs/RESEARCH.md for the current
  draft and status).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shaw
    given-names: Animesh
    alias: AnimeshShaw
repository-code: "https://github.com/AnimeshShaw/mal-agent"
url: "https://github.com/AnimeshShaw/mal-agent"
abstract: >-
  mal-agent is an evidence-grounded, agentic static malware
  analysis pipeline. Deterministic tools (PE/ELF/Mach-O parsing,
  capa capability detection, Authenticode verification, YARA
  matching, headless Ghidra decompilation, format-aware triage for
  scripts/LNK/Office/PDF, and a pretrained EMBER2024 classifier)
  produce a verdict a human can audit end to end: every claim
  traces to real tool evidence, and the classifier's decision
  authority is restricted to the file formats it was actually
  trained on. An opt-in research mode routes only the classifier's
  genuinely uncertain cases -- out-of-distribution formats,
  gray-zone scores, classifier-vs-evidence conflicts -- to a
  bounded LLM adjudicator that must cite tool-derived evidence and
  is structurally barred from treating the sample's own text as
  proof of its own innocence.
keywords:
  - malware-analysis
  - reverse-engineering
  - large-language-models
  - llm-as-judge
  - agentic-ai
  - static-analysis
  - capa
  - ghidra
  - yara
  - ember2024
  - security
